{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact NF-2 head d5ea2f75a65cd9eb8851419eaf0825aa9deae4bc on builder/mcp-boundary-nf2-20261111, all 45 artifacts, for request 9a321a0a under promise b7f2ffaa and review request d9098e2d. The head does what 9a321a0a asks under ruling e1f2ef36, with one condition met only in part. The planner decides whether that part holds the landing.\n\nThe condition met in part: \"No in-process caller reads structuredContent by string key.\" The note names the two reads that remain.\n- `checkedLocalResult` (`packages/mcp/src/views/session.ts:109-116`) checks a result from the local review callback, which is untrusted input. A key read is the right shape there, because the function is the parser that proves the type.\n- `#stoppedEarly` (`packages/mcp/src/service.ts:516`) reads `structuredContent[\"error\"]` from an untyped `CallResult`. When `isError` is true, the result is a `Failure`, and `FindingData` could give that read a type. That change is one line.\nNeither read changes behaviour.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The move. `DESCRIPTION_CHARS`, `Described`, `describeAct` and `indented` now live in `packages/mcp/src/describe.ts`. `descriptionsOf` in the Client no longer returns `describeAct`. `packages/mcp` re-exports no Client name, and each importer takes the name from its owner.\n- One typed result. `projectAnswer` in `packages/mcp/src/act-result.ts` builds the result of an act tool, `act`, `create`, `join`, `install_application`, a prepared step and the last outcome of `settle`. I compared it with the removed `#answerOf`, `#archivedSettlementOf` and the old `projectAnswer`. Every member and value is the same, apart from the ruled changes:\n  - `effects` now appears on every accepted result.\n  - An accepted install reports its custody phase, `accepted`, instead of the literal `recorded`.\n  - The accepted install gains `outboxIds`.\n  - An archived result lists its members in a new order.\n- `ACT_OUTPUT`. It `satisfies Record\u003ckeyof ActResult, JsonSchema\u003e`, and its `required` list `satisfies Record\u003cRequiredKeys\u003cActResult\u003e, true\u003e`. The `answer` and `phase` enums come from tables that satisfy `Answer[\"answer\"]` and `Phase`. A missing member fails the typecheck. Only `answer` is required now, which matches the results that carry no `sentence` and no `next`.\n- Typed call results. `Success\u003cT\u003e`, `Failure`, `CallOutcome\u003cT\u003e` and `dataOf` replace the casts in the view session and in `apps/views/src/decision.ts`. The changes in `session.ts` and `decision.ts` change types only.\n- Schema fixes. Each one narrows a schema to what its parser accepts, as 9a321a0a item 3 and e1f2ef36 ask:\n  - The scope ID pattern ends in `[aq]` and the incarnation pattern ends in `[aeimquy4]`, which matches the zero trailing bits that `isScopeId` and `isIncarnation` require.\n  - `settle` takes `membership`.\n  - `owner` uses `memberRefArg`, and `release` uses the digest pattern.\n  - `diff` takes a 40-character commit ID.\n  - `on` and `item` have a safe-integer maximum.\n  - `capability` and `step` have a 128-character maximum.\n  The audit table lists the remaining differences, all of them schemas stricter than their parsers or character bounds against byte bounds, with no code change.\n- `docs/mcp-tools.json`. By tool and field, against 33836693, the changes are: the output schema of all 59 act tools, `create` and `join`; the input schemas of the six fixed tools; and the `application_installation` description, which now says \"state, installation workflow phase\" because install results now report the custody phase.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. Main 33836693 is an ancestor, and the pushed branch equals the head. The builder's worktree is clean at the head. Against 33836693, the head changes exactly the 45 paths that the 45 artifacts cover, all at the head, none stale or retired. The head merges onto main fb354651 with no conflict.\n- Cheap checks. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings. The commit-message check passes: 17 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean.\n- The failed gate and its follow-up, under `docs/evidence-filing.md`.\n  - The gate at 95ff9a43 under `caffeinate -i` exited 1 with one Native failure, the H6 matrix in `hosted.scope.test.ts`. Every stage ran.\n  - 456c1a05 changes only that file, which nothing imports. The change resets the agent through a fresh `agentStub(bot.agent)` instead of the stub made before the held admission. Every case, assertion and deadline stays.\n  - The MCP scope compiler exited 0, and the whole Hosted file passed 24 of 24 (END 595d5a0f).\n  - I accept the follow-up as evidence for source 456c1a05. The gate stays exit 1. The earlier run at 95ff9a43 is void under ruling 45f7507b.\n- The earlier gate at e989e6ee failed 25 Native tests. 24 expected `phase: \"recorded\"` from an accepted install, and the 25th failed because an earlier test failed first. ebc4c936 changes those eleven expectations to `accepted`, and the ten files passed 31 of 31.\n- Evidence. All 38 files in the manifest match their SHA-256 values in `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence`.\n- CI, under ruling a8d2f83d. Page run 43318611822 at 9d3a4fd5 and Card run 43320873989 at e989e6ee are push events, attempt 1, completed and successful. I read both push path filters from the workflow files. No path changed from those commits to the head matches either filter.\n- I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The Client keeps the sentences and field words. MCP owns the bounded tool description, the envelope schemas and the one result type, and the build ties the published output schema to that type.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The schema changes only narrow what a host may send, and every parser still decides. Results carry no new secret. `effects` is a count, and `outboxIds` already appeared on accepted act results.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Two notes for a later head:\n\n1. The `phase` description in `ACT_OUTPUT` says \"it does not prove that the installation workflow finished\". All 59 act tools carry that sentence, but only an install has an installation workflow. The sentence belongs in the install tool's own words.\n2. The accepted and refused install paths still spread `retained`, `phase` and `next` after `projectAnswer`. Passing them through `AnswerContext` would make `projectAnswer` the only builder.\n\nThis approval authorizes no landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing and the deployment, and `MCP_ENABLED` stays off.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8c6b894308cb627a5a74a0cdae21c6816b280dde","binding":"assigned","head":"d5ea2f75a65cd9eb8851419eaf0825aa9deae4bc","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6973d0ed42c01dac4e7e97a4f40bb254adbe1515\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b7f2ffaa80883998ed89bb847397e47af5cdf471\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:14e7043741e17f1cb6691c58eeb3b4ee599a5e06","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}